House Minority Leader Nancy Pelosi is  leading a Democratic delegation into the  heart of the immigration storm tonight  they're visiting a border facility where  children are being held national  correspondent William la jeunesse is in  San Diego right now this is not about  immigration this is about humanity it's  about family it's about who we are as a  country  for days Democrats fanned out across the  country to hammer president Trump's  zero-tolerance immigration policy it's  appalling it's not American it's  unnecessary but it's also not new the  decision to prosecute any and all who  crossed the border illegally actually  began as a pilot program under President  Bush in 2006 the zero tolerance policy  is intended to deter people from  breaking the law  Manny Padilla was chief patrol agent in  Tucson when President Obama expanded  operations streamline increasing  prosecutions some 200 percent which  advocates claim helped reduce illegal  immigration today the Trump  administration makes the same case we  cannot and will not encourage people to  bring their children or other children  to the country unlawfully by giving them  immunity in the process the  administration also hopes zero tolerance  will reduce fraud we do not have the  luxury of pretending that all  individuals coming to this country as a  family unit are in fact a family  Homeland Security claims illegal  immigrants fraudulently using children  to pose as family increased 315 percent  this fiscal year exploiting a loophole  to escape deportation in prosecuting  those cases the department separated  some 1,200 children from an adult the  smugglers and traffickers know these  loop holders loopholes better than our  members of Congress critics say Trump is  separating children not to change the  law but as a bargaining chip to fund his  wall how is it possible that we don't  have a president who would rescind this  zero inhumanity policy immediately  so moments ago the administration stress  that entering the u.s. without  permission is a crime and basically the  problem is is that when you detain women  and children the courts have said that  you have to release them within 20 days  the administration wants Congress to  close that loophole so families can stay  together but when we heard Brett from  Democrats today is they want to ban this  practice and they believe that family  should be handled administratively not  criminally buckey's William Lodge nest  in San Diego William thank you
 

